<main class="pc" data-product-depth="primordocciput"><p class="pc-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS / Research / Author's concept</p><h1>CRANIO research architecture.</h1><p class="pc-lead">Primordocciput is the author's primary cranial reference concept. The research layer connects it to configuration, observation and measurement questions.</p><div class="pc-steps" role="navigation" aria-label="Research"><a href="../primordocciput/" aria-current="page">Primordocciput</a><a href="../c0-c1/">C0–C1–C2</a><a href="../logbook/">Logbook</a></div><section class="pc-section"><h2>Research map</h2><div class="pc-research-map"><article class="pc-card"><h3>C0–C1–C2</h3><p>Anatomical landmarks and configuration research.</p><a class="pc-link" href="../c0-c1/">C0–C1–C2 ↗</a></article><article class="pc-card"><h3>Primordocciput</h3><p>The author's primary cranial reference concept.</p><a class="pc-link" href="../primordocciput/">Primordocciput ↗</a></article><article class="pc-card"><h3>THE ELECTRIC HUMAN</h3><p>Research questions about bioelectrical properties; concept layer.</p><a class="pc-link" href="../../technology/vita-wellness/#electric">THE ELECTRIC HUMAN ↗</a></article><article class="pc-card"><h3>Spine Bilateral Mapping</h3><p>Interactive technology demonstration and integration questions.</p><a class="pc-link" href="../../technology/vita-wellness/">Spine Bilateral Mapping ↗</a></article><article class="pc-card"><h3>Logbook</h3><p>Open questions, observations and the next step.</p><a class="pc-link" href="../logbook/">Logbook ↗</a></article></div></section><section class="pc-section"><h2>Four kinds of research information</h2><div class="pc-grid"><details class="pc-card"><summary>Observed</summary><p>Describe what is visible in a particular context.</p></details><details class="pc-card"><summary>Measured</summary><p>Record units, method, conditions and uncertainty.</p></details><details class="pc-card"><summary>Reported</summary><p>Preserve the source of the subjective report.</p></details><details class="pc-card"><summary>Research concept</summary><p>State the model, question and possible test.</p></details></div><div class="pc-actions"><a class="pc-button primary" href="../start/">Discuss research collaboration</a><a class="pc-button" href="../technology/">Technology</a></div></section><section class="pc-section"><details class="pc-legacy"><summary>Existing materials</summary><div class="wrap"><article class="article"><div class="crumbs">CRANIO / Primordocciput — The Primary Cranial Reference</div><h2>Primordocciput</h2><p class="lead">A CRANIO concept for understanding the skull base and upper-neck relationship as a primary reference.</p><section class="section"><div class="eyebrow">Primordocciput — The Primary Cranial Reference</div><h2>Primordocciput</h2><p class="lead">A CRANIO concept for understanding the skull base and upper-neck relationship as a primary reference.</p></section><section class="section"><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3>Observation</h3><p>Separate observation from interpretation.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Context</h3><p>Context makes a state comparable over time.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Verification</h3><p>Before, after, context and time remain visible.</p></div></div></section><div class="actions"><a class="btn dark" href="../start/">Start an observation</a><a class="btn" href="../explore/">Explore</a></div></article></div></details></section></main>